  "term": "EMDR",
  "definition": "EMDR is a technique intended to help the brain process disturbing memories and experiences through stimulation thought to resemble neural activity during REM sleep. It uses guided side-to-side eye movements or alternating taps to promote information processing and connections among neural networks.",
